1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,820
Why do reindeer eyes turn blue in winter?

2
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,740
In summer they shine gold.

3
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,420
In winter... deep blue.

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,720
Behind each eye is a mirror that bounces

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,030
light back, for a second chance to see.

6
00:00:12,330 --> 00:00:14,250
But in the Arctic winter the sun hides

7
00:00:14,250 --> 00:00:17,110
for weeks, so their pupils stay wide open.

8
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,720
Fluid can't drain properly.

9
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,260
Pressure builds, and squeezes the mirror's

10
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,730
tiny fibres together.

11
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:25,370
Packed tighter, it reflects blue, the

12
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:26,210
colour of twilight.

13
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:29,070
Less light escapes, so they see more in

14
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:29,530
the dark.
